{"qid": "77410975", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "How to use Langchain text splitter to reduce tokens in my text", "answer": "The text splitter is designed to split text into chunks based on the tokenizer used by the language model. In your case, you are using the RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter, which splits text into chunks of 1000 tokens with an overlap of 50 tokens. However, this may not be sufficient for your 300-inch PDF, which exceeds the maximum token limit of the OpenAI API. To improve this, you can try using a larger chunk size or a different tokenizer, such as tiktoken. Additionally, you can use the MapReduceChain to combine the chunks and input longer texts into the prompt. Here is an example of how you can use the MapReduceChain: ", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/pdf_qa.ipynb_0_6943", "langchain/libs/langchain/langchain/chains/mapreduce.py_0_4092", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_0_7093"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/pdf_qa.ipynb_0_6943", "langchain/libs/langchain/langchain/chains/mapreduce.py_0_4092", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_0_7093"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 0.75, "context_recall": 0.06451612903225806, "nuggets": ["The text splitter breaks down text into chunks based on tokens and new lines, with chunk size specified by the user.", "The purpose of the text splitter is to divide documents into smaller chunks to retrieve the most relevant text pieces.", "The text splitter does not increase the amount of text that can be input into the prompt but helps fit relevant information within the token limit.", "Printing data before and after splitting can help visualize the effect of the text splitter."], "nuggets_present": null, "nugget_judge_ok": null, "citations": [{"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/pdf_qa.ipynb_0_6943", "sup