{"qid": "77782167", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'langchain_openai'", "answer": "The error is due to the fact that `langchain_openai` is not a part of the `langchain` package. According to the documentation, `pip install langchain` only installs the necessary modules for `langchain-community` and `langchain-core`, but not `langchain-openai`. You need to install `langchain-openai` separately using `pip install langchain-openai`.", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/functions.ipynb_0_7018", "langchain/libs/cli/langchain_cli/integration_template/integration_template/retrievers.py_0_2512", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/parallel.ipynb_0_7120"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/functions.ipynb_0_7018", "langchain/libs/cli/langchain_cli/integration_template/integration_template/retrievers.py_0_2512", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/parallel.ipynb_0_7120"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 0.0, "context_recall": 0.0, "nuggets": ["The `ModuleNotFoundError` is due to the incorrect module path for `ChatOpenAI`.", "The correct module to import `ChatOpenAI` from is `langchain_community.chat_models`."], "nuggets_present": null, "nugget_judge_ok": null, "citations": [{"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/functions.ipynb_0_7018", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": null, "relevant_in_qrels": false, "judged_in_qrels": true}, {"doc_id": "langchain/libs/cli/langchain_cli/integration_template/integration_template/retrievers.py_0_2512", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": null, "relevant_in_qrels": false, "judged_in_qrels": false}, {"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/parallel.ipynb_0_7120", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_o